[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-edd4a7fb-8162-47ce-a03c-23987d540ae4\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research Papers</p><strong>Wed 19 Nov 2025 12:20 - 12:30 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/ase-2025/ase-2025-venue-grand-hall-2\" class=\"room-link navigate\">Grand Hall 2</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/ase-2025/ase-2025-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Web &amp; Mobile Systems 1</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/jacquesklein\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Jacques Klein</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"edd4a7fb-8162-47ce-a03c-23987d540ae4\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>Automated Detection of Web Application Navigation Barriers for Screen Reader Users</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>An estimated 43.3 million people worldwide live with blindness and rely on screen readers (SRs) to access the web. To support accessible development, software teams often rely on automated tools like WAVE and Lighthouse to detect accessibility issues. However, these tools primarily rely on static rule-based analysis and are largely limited to detecting labeling errors relevant to screen reader users. They fail to capture dynamic accessibility issues\u2014specifically, whether user interface (UI) elements can be located and activated using a screen reader, which is essential for accessing core webpage functionality. To address this gap, we present A11yNavigator, an automated accessibility testing tool that simulates screen reader navigation to detect UI elements that cannot be either (1) located or (2) activated via the screen reader. A11yNavigator leverages NVDA, one of the most widely used screen readers, and supports three common navigation strategies: Tab, Arrow, and Quick Navigation keys. We evaluate A11yNavigator across 26 real-world websites and demonstrate its effectiveness in uncovering issues missed by existing tools. Our results highlight its high precision and recall in detecting barriers that go beyond static analysis.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/shubhijain\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Shubhi Jain\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/shubhijain/682b4542-2921-41e4-b85b-d46295c92655/micro-avatar?1783978877000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Shubhi Jain<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, Irvine</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/syedfatiulhuq\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Syed Fatiul Huq\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/syedfatiulhuq/d2bea035-ca6f-4be2-97e5-04fa98b421c8/micro-avatar?1783980256000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Syed Fatiul <span class=\"name-visual-sep\"></span>Huq<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, Irvine</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/ziyaohe\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Ziyao He\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/ziyaohe/680b208f-4311-4201-ba9d-573884559f30/micro-avatar?1783976129000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Ziyao He<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California, Irvine</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/ase-2025/sammalek\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"Sam Malek\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getProfileImage/sammalek/167841b3-c278-45c1-ad36-3ab5f71db112/micro-avatar?1783979052000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Sam Malek<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">University of California at Irvine</span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><small>United States</small></h5></div></div></a></div></div></div><br></div><div class=\"modal-footer\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/details/ase-2025/ase-2025-papers/192/Automated-Detection-of-Web-Application-Navigation-Barriers-for-Screen-Reader-Users\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"btn btn-default navigate\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-new-window\"></span> All Details</a></span><a href=\"#\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"btn btn-default\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span> Close</a></div></div></div></div>"},{ "action": "runscript", "value": "$('#modal-edd4a7fb-8162-47ce-a03c-23987d540ae4').modal({ backdrop: 'static', keyboard: true}